    a: "<b>Diagnosis:</b> <b>Inferior STEMI</b> (RCA territory — leads II, III, aVF)<br><b>Management:</b><ul><li>Activate cath lab immediately — goal <b>door-to-balloon time &lt; 90 minutes</b></li><li>Aspirin 325 mg + P2Y12 inhibitor (<b>ticagrelor</b> or clopidogrel)</li><li>Anticoagulation (heparin or bivalirudin)</li><li>Check <b>right-sided leads (V4R)</b> — inferior STEMI has ~40% association with <b>RV infarct</b>; avoid nitrates and diuretics if RV involved</li></ul><b>If PCI unavailable within 120 min:</b> administer <b>fibrinolytics</b> (tPA, tenecteplase) within 30 min of presentation (door-to-needle &lt; 30 min)."
