    a: "<b>Diagnosis:</b> <b>Acute pericarditis</b><br><b>Classic features:</b><ul><li>Pleuritic, positional chest pain — worse supine, better leaning forward</li><li>ECG: diffuse saddle-shaped ST elevations + <b>PR depression</b> (most specific finding)</li><li>Pericardial friction rub on auscultation</li></ul><b>Treatment:</b><ul><li><b>NSAIDs</b> (ibuprofen 600 mg TID × 2 weeks) — first-line</li><li>Add <b>colchicine</b> 0.5 mg BID × 3 months to reduce recurrence</li><li>Restrict strenuous exercise until symptom-free</li><li>Avoid NSAIDs post-MI (risk of myocardial thinning)</li></ul><b>Workup:</b> echo to rule out effusion; troponin to assess for myopericarditis."
