    a: "<b>Diagnosis:</b> <b>Acute ischemic stroke</b><br><b>Eligibility for IV alteplase (tPA):</b><ul><li>Onset &lt; <b>4.5 hours</b> (she qualifies at 2 hours)</li><li>No hemorrhage on CT, no recent major surgery, no active bleeding, no prior ICH</li><li>BP must be &lt; 185/110 before tPA — lower with labetalol or nicardipine</li></ul><b>Dosing:</b> alteplase 0.9 mg/kg IV (max 90 mg); 10% as bolus over 1 min, remainder over 60 min<br><b>Thrombectomy:</b> if large vessel occlusion (LVO) on CTA, eligible up to <b>24 hours</b> from onset (with favorable imaging)<br><b>Post-tPA:</b> no anticoagulants or antiplatelets for 24h; target BP &lt; 180/105 mmHg<br><b>Do NOT aggressively lower BP</b> in acute ischemic stroke unless giving tPA (permissive hypertension preserves penumbra)."
