    a: "<b>Diagnosis:</b> <b>Acute decompensated heart failure (HFrEF)</b><br><b>Acute management (LMNOP mnemonic):</b><ul><li><b>L</b>asix (furosemide IV): 1–2.5× oral dose IV; monitor urine output, BMP daily</li><li><b>M</b>orphine: cautiously for dyspnea/anxiety (optional; may worsen outcomes)</li><li><b>N</b>itrates (nitroglycerin): vasodilation → reduces preload; useful if SBP &gt; 90</li><li><b>O</b>xygen: keep SpO2 &gt; 94%; CPAP if cardiogenic pulmonary edema</li><li><b>P</b>ositioning: head of bed elevated</li></ul><b>Avoid:</b> NSAIDs (sodium retention), CCBs (negative inotropy in HFrEF), thiazolidinediones<br><b>Chronic HFrEF therapy:</b><ul><li>ACE inhibitor/ARB/ARNI + beta-blocker (carvedilol, metoprolol succinate) + mineralocorticoid antagonist (spironolactone) + SGLT2 inhibitor (dapagliflozin)</li></ul>"
